				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Cocoon): Implement full VS Code dialog and language service APIs\n\nComplete the vscode API shim in APIFactory by routing core dialog and language services to Mountain via Vine gRPC.\n\nDialog APIs:\n- showInformationMessage, showErrorMessage, showWarningMessage now send notifications to Mountain for native OS dialog display\n- showQuickPick and showInputBox implemented with full request/response handling\n- createOutputChannel now creates managed channels with append/appendLine/clear/show/dispose operations\n- withProgress now creates progress handles and reports progress via gRPC\n- createTerminal creates native terminal instances with input/output handling\n\nLanguage Services:\n- Implement complete vscode.languages namespace with 25+ provider registrations\n- Each register*Provider method assigns unique handle and routes registration to Mountain via sendNotification\n- Provider callbacks stored in Map for lookup when Mountain sends provide_* RPCs back\n- Full implementations for hover, completion, definition, references, code actions, document symbols, workspace symbols, renaming, formatting, signature help, code lenses, folding ranges, semantic tokens, inlay hints, type hierarchy, call hierarchy, document links, color provider, and more\n- createDiagnosticCollection now maintains a real Map of URI -> Diagnostics\n\nThis enables VS Code extensions running in Cocoon to access native OS dialogs, progress reporting, terminal integration, and full language server protocol support.",
			"SHA": "57d8edec5d13d4984a83f3c47ad093f9ee2870a9"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-04T07:15:55Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				274,
				1
			],
			"Message": "docs(Cocoon): benefit-focused README rewrite\n\nReplace verbose technical documentation with outcome-first copy matching the website's goal-oriented direction.\n\nThe old README led with feature lists and architectural deep-dives. The new version opens with the core problem statement (VS Code's single event loop limitation), followed by what Cocoon gives you: supervised fiber isolation, automatic timeout/restart, and concurrent extension activation.\n\nReferences: 4b42f88c5a671ffdbbdc04a08392808931f655fe (previous README rewrite)",
			"SHA": "81e1b082caeb47f6db3fd96ade15966c85963514"
